00:03:47.005 --> 00:03:49.138
- [Voiceover] @BottledGrapes asks,

00:03:49.138 --> 00:03:50.775
"We have a brick and mortar shop.

00:03:50.775 --> 00:03:53.933
"In today's technology
world, how important

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:57.164
"is location, location, location?"

00:03:58.387 --> 00:04:00.490
- Location, location, location.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:04.181
So I think the 1998 version of me

00:04:04.181 --> 00:04:06.446
would have said, "Oh, it
doesn't matter as much anymore,

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:09.929
"in 20 years, 10 years,
it'll be all e-com."

00:04:09.929 --> 00:04:11.810
As the gray hairs have come in,

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.026
I recognize things take longer to evolve.

00:04:15.026 --> 00:04:17.962
I would say location matters
tremendously still today,

00:04:17.962 --> 00:04:20.204
and very much over the next 10 years.

00:04:20.204 --> 00:04:22.990
Do I think 20 years from
today that we will be

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:26.357
in a 30, 40, 50, 60, 70% e-com world

00:04:26.357 --> 00:04:29.097
and things will be overpriced by location

00:04:29.097 --> 00:04:30.165
in a physical world?

00:04:30.165 --> 00:04:31.233
I do.

00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:32.545
But I would say for the next half decade

00:04:32.545 --> 00:04:36.179
to a full decade, location is
still enormously important.

00:04:36.179 --> 00:04:39.163
People still go to stores,
people still drive their cars,

00:04:39.163 --> 00:04:42.088
people still are in dense
areas where a great location

00:04:42.088 --> 00:04:46.059
really matters, and so
I would highly recommend

00:04:46.059 --> 00:04:49.111
respecting the bricks
and mortars location.

00:04:49.111 --> 00:04:51.411
Now, that being said,
there's a more interesting

00:04:51.411 --> 00:04:53.873
variation of this answer, which is

00:04:53.873 --> 00:04:58.873
today's technology world,
are you able to just rely on

00:04:58.876 --> 00:05:01.535
bricks and mortars location,
location, location,

00:05:01.535 --> 00:05:03.124
and that is a big fat no.

00:05:03.124 --> 00:05:05.274
If you were not thinking about your e-com,

00:05:05.274 --> 00:05:07.503
your mobile strategy, your app culture,

00:05:07.503 --> 00:05:10.045
your content strategy,
your social strategy,

00:05:10.045 --> 00:05:13.409
your digital strategy,
you are just basically

00:05:13.409 --> 00:05:16.437
just setting the game plan in motion

00:05:16.437 --> 00:05:18.366
to the demise of your business,

00:05:18.366 --> 00:05:20.408
and so location still matters,

00:05:20.408 --> 00:05:22.604
but the investment into the future,

00:05:22.604 --> 00:05:25.924
especially with the acceleration
and the exponential growth

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:28.594
of our culture around digital behavior

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:29.905
is an enormous mistake.

00:05:29.905 --> 00:05:31.358
So you need both.

00:05:31.358 --> 00:05:33.204
That I highly believe in.

00:05:33.204 --> 00:05:34.562
Who needs that room?

00:05:34.562 --> 00:05:36.373
What?

00:05:36.373 --> 00:05:38.289
I do?

00:05:38.289 --> 00:05:40.975
That's fine, I'm finishing my show.

00:05:40.975 --> 00:05:41.862
Alright, go ahead.

00:05:42.962 --> 00:05:45.632
- [Voiceover] Anthony asks,
"Is standing your ground

00:05:45.632 --> 00:05:47.838
"during negotiations something that is in

00:05:47.838 --> 00:05:50.561
"someone's DNA, or can it be taught?"

00:05:51.736 --> 00:05:55.164
- Anthony, I think it is probably

00:05:55.164 --> 00:05:56.882
a very strong combination of both.

00:05:56.882 --> 00:06:01.972
I, for a long time, up
until July 7th, 2014,

00:06:01.972 --> 00:06:04.173
believed that almost everything was DNA.

00:06:04.173 --> 00:06:06.275
But something that does
not come natural to me

00:06:06.275 --> 00:06:08.898
is taking care of my health, right?

00:06:08.898 --> 00:06:11.603
And what I've done is I've hacked,

00:06:11.603 --> 00:06:13.786
and I've taught myself, and
now is it my own behavior?

00:06:13.786 --> 00:06:14.923
No, I have a babysitter.

00:06:14.923 --> 00:06:15.667
His name's Mike.

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:16.851
You've seen him, you've heard of him.

00:06:16.851 --> 00:06:20.067
So I do think certain things can be taught

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:22.528
to a degree, meaning, for example,

00:06:22.528 --> 00:06:23.840
I've been playing basketball more often

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:25.672
and my jump shot is getting better.

00:06:25.672 --> 00:06:27.694
I've brought back my running jumper.

00:06:27.694 --> 00:06:29.378
Staphon knows what I'm talking about.

00:06:29.378 --> 00:06:33.184
And so I do think negotiating skills

00:06:33.184 --> 00:06:35.157
is something that can be taught,

00:06:35.157 --> 00:06:37.872
but it would be naive to not recognize

00:06:37.872 --> 00:06:40.394
that some people are just
born with that talent.

00:06:40.394 --> 00:06:43.457
So probably, like every
answer to every question

00:06:43.457 --> 00:06:46.257
in the world, the answer is both.

00:06:46.257 --> 00:06:50.030
A little bit of training and building up,

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:52.131
I think I taught AJ to
be a better negotiator.

00:06:52.131 --> 00:06:53.930
I think he naturally had it in him,

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.707
but I think there was some
teaching moments there

00:06:55.707 --> 00:06:59.097
at the garage sales of New Jersey, and so

00:06:59.097 --> 00:07:02.011
I actually think the way it can be taught

00:07:02.011 --> 00:07:03.322
is more through osmosis.

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:04.925
I think surrounding yourself

00:07:04.925 --> 00:07:07.189
with those kind of strong negotiators

00:07:07.189 --> 00:07:09.744
is better than watching a video about it

00:07:09.744 --> 00:07:11.137
or reading about how to do it,

00:07:11.137 --> 00:07:14.655
and so I think learned
behavior by feeling it,

00:07:14.655 --> 00:07:16.942
not just by reading it, is the way to go.

00:07:16.942 --> 00:07:18.091
So I would say both.

00:07:18.091 --> 00:07:19.357
I would say 80 20.

00:07:19.357 --> 00:07:21.574
I think 80% of the equation is natural,

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:24.001
but I do think you can be taught 20% lift

00:07:24.001 --> 00:07:25.719
off of where your natural place

00:07:25.719 --> 00:07:27.321
in the lexicon of negotiation,

00:07:27.321 --> 00:07:29.545
or maybe anything else, really is.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:36.425
- [Voiceover] Dmitry asks, "How
do you celebrate victories?"

00:07:37.582 --> 00:07:40.087
- Dmitry, I took this question
for a very specific reason,

00:07:40.087 --> 00:07:42.818
because this is absolutely, no question,

00:07:42.818 --> 00:07:47.203
one of the flaws of my being.

00:07:47.203 --> 00:07:50.698
I am terrible at celebrating victories.

00:07:50.698 --> 00:07:52.625
It is actually quite sad in some ways

00:07:52.625 --> 00:07:53.995
if you decide to look at it that way,

00:07:53.995 --> 00:07:56.132
or a very strong winner's mentatlity

00:07:56.132 --> 00:07:57.490
which is how I like to look at it,

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.464
but the truth is I stink at it.

00:07:59.464 --> 00:08:01.890
As a matter of fact,
one of the bigger flaws

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.851
that I think I'm creating
at VaynerMedia as a culture

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:06.964
is that we don't celebrate our wins.

00:08:06.964 --> 00:08:08.485
We land big new accounts.

00:08:08.485 --> 00:08:09.747
We grow like crazy.

00:08:09.747 --> 00:08:10.946
We win awards.

00:08:10.946 --> 00:08:11.770
Hush, hush.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:12.548
Nothing.

00:08:12.548 --> 00:08:15.297
No chest pounding, and I
think it's interesting,

00:08:15.297 --> 00:08:17.047
because when you look at me as a character

00:08:17.047 --> 00:08:19.604
and you look how I roll,
for all the humble bragging

00:08:19.604 --> 00:08:21.612
and the outright bragging, and the ego

00:08:21.612 --> 00:08:24.074
and the confidence that I spew out there,

00:08:24.074 --> 00:08:25.711
it's funny.

00:08:25.711 --> 00:08:27.962
It's always in hindsight,
and it's in showmanship,

00:08:27.962 --> 00:08:32.154
it's not in reality, meaning,
I celebrate victories poorly.

00:08:32.154 --> 00:08:34.859
For example, the New York
Rangers and the New York Yankees

00:08:34.859 --> 00:08:36.798
have both won championships for me.

00:08:36.798 --> 00:08:38.107
They won their championship.

00:08:38.107 --> 00:08:40.861
I was very happy for
about a couple of hours.

00:08:40.861 --> 00:08:45.297
No parades, no next day taking
off and like soaking it in.

00:08:45.297 --> 00:08:48.290
I won, and I moved on,
and I stopped caring.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.266
I'm gonna say it here first.

00:08:50.266 --> 00:08:52.646
I've really never said this
out loud outside of my family.

00:08:52.646 --> 00:08:54.620
I am completely convinced
that if the New York Jets

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.593
win a Super Bowl before I buy them,

00:08:56.593 --> 00:08:59.310
that I will no longer
like the Jets that much

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.435
and all my energy will
then be transplanted

00:09:01.435 --> 00:09:04.220
100,000% into the 
New York Knicks.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.286
I firmly believe that.

00:09:05.286 --> 00:09:07.132
I just completely believe that.

00:09:07.132 --> 00:09:09.025
I love the climb.

00:09:09.025 --> 00:09:13.274
I celebrate victories in a very soft,

00:09:13.274 --> 00:09:15.898
non appropriate way.

00:09:15.898 --> 00:09:17.865
I'm really dissapointed

00:09:17.865 --> 00:09:20.500
in the way that I celebrate victories.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.230
It's something that I want to work on

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:25.795
because smelling the
roses is an important part

00:09:25.795 --> 00:09:28.418
of growing and living, and it's just

00:09:28.418 --> 00:09:29.733
not something I'm good at.

00:09:30.969 --> 00:09:32.444
- [Voiceover] Corey asks,

00:09:32.444 --> 00:09:35.626
"What should I get my
mom for Mother's Day?"

00:09:36.411 --> 00:09:39.662
- Corey, I think the big
strategy for Mother's Day 2015

00:09:39.662 --> 00:09:41.763
is for people that are
watching the show to recognize

00:09:41.763 --> 00:09:44.190
a lot of their moms are on Pinterest,

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:46.696
and that they should go to
their mom's Pinterest board

00:09:46.696 --> 00:09:48.927
and see what mama has been pinning

00:09:48.927 --> 00:09:50.819
and buy her something from there,

00:09:50.819 --> 00:09:53.130
and so if you're not
lucky enough to have that,

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.044
where your mama is pinning,
then I would highly recommend

00:09:56.044 --> 00:09:59.862
looking at her social media and looking at

00:09:59.862 --> 00:10:02.278
what she's tweeting or Facebooking,

00:10:02.278 --> 00:10:03.579
which will not be as good as Pinterest,

00:10:03.579 --> 00:10:05.262
but you might find the
diamond in the rough,

00:10:05.262 --> 00:10:07.468
and then, if you can't do that,

00:10:07.468 --> 00:10:09.151
the move that so many don't do

00:10:09.151 --> 00:10:11.462
that I highly recommend for
you and the VaynerNation,

00:10:11.462 --> 00:10:14.248
is to randomly call
your mom's best friend,

00:10:14.248 --> 00:10:15.902
the one that you might have
not talked to in a long time,

00:10:15.902 --> 00:10:18.608
or it might be your aunt that
you only talk to once a year

00:10:18.608 --> 00:10:20.532
to wish a happy birthday
or whoever it may be,

00:10:20.532 --> 00:10:25.474
and ask her what, or him,
what you should buy your mom,

00:10:25.474 --> 00:10:28.987
because friends know, and I
think that would be thoughtful.

00:10:28.987 --> 00:10:31.692
I think putting in the effort
to try to really buy your mom

00:10:31.692 --> 00:10:34.574
something she wants for
Mother's Day is the move.

00:10:34.574 --> 00:10:36.082
I feel like I've inspired

00:10:36.082 --> 00:10:38.069
three or four of you,
because that's about as high

00:10:38.069 --> 00:10:40.368
as I think this will go,
but that makes me happy,

00:10:40.368 --> 00:10:41.842
because three to four of your moms

00:10:41.842 --> 00:10:42.837
are gonna have a better Mother's Day

00:10:42.837 --> 00:10:45.254
because of the #AskGaryVee Show.

00:10:50.084 --> 00:10:52.650
- [Voiceover] Dr. Julie
asks, "As VaynerMedia

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:55.402
"continues to grow, what is the one thing

00:10:55.402 --> 00:10:58.403
"the company has done to
keep the culture hungry?"

00:11:00.115 --> 00:11:04.190
- Doc, everything stems from the top.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:08.660
My hunger level is so
intense it's crippling,

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:12.317
and so, because of that, the
culture continues to be hungry

00:11:12.317 --> 00:11:14.709
because I will suffocate the culture

00:11:14.709 --> 00:11:16.602
to allow nothing else to creep in.

00:11:16.602 --> 00:11:19.642
No complacency, no
celebrating the victories

00:11:19.642 --> 00:11:22.244
allows you to stay really damn hungry.

00:11:22.244 --> 00:11:24.392
We've haven't accomplished shit yet,

00:11:24.392 --> 00:11:26.122
